# NOAH - Archive utility

Keep NOAH.COM and its matching NOAH.OVL together. On the experimental
set, enter C0: before running the following commands.

## Help libraries

To create a help library from the loose subjects in D0, use:

```text
NOAH /ADD D0:TOOLS.LBR D0:*.HLP
NOAH /TEST D0:TOOLS.LBR
A0:HELP /S=D0:TOOLS.LBR
```

Include an _INDEX.HLP for an authored menu. If you omit it, HELP lists
the topics in archive order. See [choosing a help source](HELP.HLP#choosing-a-source).

## Listing members

```text
NOAH /LIST D0:TOOLS.LBR
NOAH /LIST D0:HELP.ARK
```

Use /TEST to check archive data. To extract to another user area, type:

```text
NOAH /EXTRACT D0:TOOLS.LBR D3:
```

## Updating members

```text
NOAH /ADD D0:TOOLS.LBR D0:FOO.HLP
NOAH /REMOVE D0:TOOLS.LBR OLD.HLP
NOAH /COMPACT D0:TOOLS.LBR
```

/ADD inserts a subject or offers to replace an existing member.
/COMPACT reclaims unused archive space. Keep any recovery files
reported after an interrupted update.
